.TH mbpy_grdplot 1 "12 September 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbpy_grdplot\fP \- Create an executable shellscript which will generate
a GMT modern-mode map of gridded data in a GMT grid file or image data in
a georeferenced image file.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbpy_grdplot\fP \fB\-I\fP\fIgrid\fP [\fB\-O\fP\fIroot\fP]
[\fB\-\-format\fP\fIfmt\fP]
[\fB\-\-title\fP\fItext\fP]
[\fB\-\-colorbar\-label\fP\fItext\fP]
[\fB\-\-dpi\fP\fIdpi\fP]
[\fB\-X\fP] [\fB\-V\fP]
.br
[\fB\-R\fP\fIxmin/xmax/ymin/ymax\fP]
[\fB\-J\fP\fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-P\fP\fIpagesize\fP]
[\fB\-\-portrait\fP | \fB\-\-landscape\fP]
[\fB\-\-scale\-location\fP\fI{l,r,t,b}\fP]
[\fB\-\-tick\-info\fP\fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-\-length\-scale\fP\fIspec\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-color\-mode\fP\fI{1-7}\fP]
[\fB\-\-no\-color\-fill\fP]
[\fB\-W\fP\fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-D\fP]
[\fB\-Y\fP]
[\fB\-\-stretch\-color\fP]
[\fB\-Z\fP\fIzmin/zmax\fP]
[\fB\-\-data\-scale\fP\fIfactor\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-magnitude\fP\fIval\fP]
[\fB\-\-azimuth\fP\fIdeg\fP]
[\fB\-\-elevation\fP\fIdeg\fP]
[\fB\-\-shade\-flip\fP]
[\fB\-\-intensity\-file\fP\fIgrid\fP]
[\fB\-\-stretch\-shade\fP]
.br
[\fB\-C\fP[\fIinterval\fP]]
[\fB\-\-contour\-file\fP\fIgrid\fP]
[\fB\-\-contour\-annotation\fP\fIinterval\fP]
[\fB\-\-contour\-pen\fP\fIpen\fP]
[\fB\-\-contour\-gap\fP\fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-\-contour\-cut\fP\fIval\fP]
[\fB\-\-contour\-tick\fP[\fIspacing\fP]]
.br
[\fB\-\-coast\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-resolution\fP\fI{f,h,i,l,c}\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-dry\-fill\fP\fIcolor\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-wet\-fill\fP\fIcolor\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-lake\-fill\fP\fIcolor\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-river\fP\fIcolor\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-boundary\fP\fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-pen\fP\fIpen\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-xy\-overlay\fP\fIfile\fP[\fI:fill=..\fP][\fI:symbol=..\fP][\fI:pen=..\fP]]
[\fB\-\-text\fP\fIlon/lat/size/angle/font/justify/text\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-nav\-file\fP\fIdatalist\fP]
[\fB\-\-nav\-format\fP\fIfmt\fP]
[\fB\-\-nav\-ticks\fP\fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-\-ping\-ticks\fP\fItick/annot/len\fP]
[\fB\-\-nav\-pen\fP\fIpen\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-gmt\-default\fP\fIparam/value\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbpy_grdplot\fP is a Python/PyGMT-era replacement for the Perl macro
\fBmbm_grdplot\fP. It reads a grid (or, in \fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 6/7, a
georeferenced or plain image file) and generates an executable
shellscript of \fBGMT\fP \fBmodern mode\fP commands (\fBgmt begin\fP /
\fBgmt end\fP, without classic mode's manual \fB\-K\fP/\fB\-O\fP
bookkeeping) which, when run, produces a map of that data. Several
styles of plots can be generated, including color fill maps, contour
maps, color fill maps overlaid with contours, shaded relief color maps,
slope magnitude maps, coastline overlays, swath navigation/ping-number
overlays, text labels, and xy data in lines or symbols.

The plot is scaled to fit the specified page size using the same
page-layout, projection-fitting, and color-palette heuristics as
\fBmbm_grdplot\fP, so the two macros produce visually equivalent maps.
Unlike \fBmbm_grdplot\fP's single-letter \fB\-M\fP\fIsub\fP\fB:\fP\fIsub\fP\fB:\fP...
grammar for coastline/navigation/contour/xy tuning, \fBmbpy_grdplot\fP
exposes each of those as its own descriptive long option (see OPTIONS
below); most options are also available as classic \fBmbm_grdplot\fP-style
single-letter flags where a natural equivalent exists.

\fBmbpy_grdplot\fP requires \fBGMT\fP 6 or later (modern mode) and a
Python 3 interpreter. It depends on four sibling support modules
(\fBmbpy_layout.py\fP, \fBmbpy_color.py\fP, \fBmbpy_misc.py\fP,
\fBmbpy_grdplot_script.py\fP) installed alongside it; the first three
are shared with the companion macros \fBmbpy_grd3dplot\fP and
\fBmbpy_histplot\fP.

Unlike \fBmbm_grdplot\fP, the generated script does not include any
step to display the plot on screen, and does not need a separate
\fBgmt psconvert\fP step to rasterize the output -- GMT modern mode's
own \fBgmt figure\fP/\fBgmt end\fP machinery renders directly to the
format requested with \fB\-\-format\fP.

