.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-I\fP, \fB\-\-input\fP \fIgrid\fP
Input grid file (or image file, for \fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 6/7). Required.
.TP
.B \-O\fP, \fB\-\-output\fP \fIroot\fP
Output root name; the generated script is \fIroot\fP\fB.sh\fP, the plot
is \fIroot\fP\fB.\fP\fIfmt\fP, and (unless \fB\-W\fP names an existing
\&.cpt file) the color palette is \fIroot\fP\fB.cpt\fP. Default: the
input grid's basename with its extension removed.
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIfmt\fP
Output format passed to \fBgmt figure\fP: \fBpdf\fP, \fBpng\fP,
\fBps\fP, \fBjpg\fP, \fBtif\fP, \fBeps\fP, ... Default \fBpdf\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-title \fItext\fP
Plot title, placed above the map frame.
.TP
.B \-\-colorbar\-label \fItext\fP
Label for the color scale bar (the second half of \fBmbm_grdplot\fP's
\fB\-L\fP\fItitle\fP\fB:\fP\fIlabel\fP). Default \fBz\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-dpi \fIdpi\fP
Rendering resolution: both \fBgrdimage\fP's own \fB\-E\fP\fIdpi\fP and
the final raster's resolution (via \fBgmt figure\fP).
.TP
.B \-X\fP, \fB\-\-execute\fP
Run the generated script immediately after writing it.
.TP
.B \-V\fP, \fB\-\-verbose\fP
Print the generated script's path and a one-line summary.
.TP
.B \-R\fP, \fB\-\-region \fIxmin/xmax/ymin/ymax\fP
Plot region. Default: the grid's own bounds.
.TP
.B \-J\fP, \fB\-\-projection \fIspec\fP
GMT map projection/scale spec, e.g. \fBm1.0\fP (Mercator, 1 inch/degree),
\fBx0.02\fP (linear, 0.02 inch/unit), \fBXd6i\fP (linear, 6 inch width).
Default: an auto-fit Mercator (geographic grids) or linear (all others)
projection chosen to fill the page.
.TP
.B \-P\fP, \fB\-\-pagesize \fIsize\fP
Page size code: \fBa\fP\-\fBf\fP, \fBe1\fP (US sizes), \fBa0\fP\-\fBa10\fP,
\fBb0\fP\-\fBb10\fP, \fBc0\fP\-\fBc7\fP (ISO/architectural), or \fBm1\fP\-\fBm6\fP
(large-format). Default \fBa\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-portrait\fP, \fB\-\-landscape
Force the page orientation instead of choosing automatically based on
the plot's aspect ratio.
.TP
.B \-\-scale\-location \fI{l,r,t,b}\fP
Color scale bar placement: left, right, top, or bottom. Default \fBb\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-tick\-info \fIspec\fP
Raw \fB\-B\fP basemap tick-interval spec, overriding the automatically
computed one.
.TP
.B \-\-length\-scale \fIspec\fP
A GMT distance (map) scale bar spec, passed as \fB\-L\fP\fIspec\fP on
\fBgmt basemap\fP, e.g. \fBfx10/2/32.70/5.0+lkm\fP (\fBmbm_grdplot\fP's
\fB\-MGL\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-color\-mode \fI{1-7}\fP
1 plain color fill; 2 color shaded relief (synthetic illumination); 3
color shaded by a supplied intensity grid; 4 color fill of slope
magnitude; 5 color shaded by slope magnitude; 6 image plot using an
image's own embedded georeferencing; 7 image plot placed using
\fB\-\-region\fP bounds (no georeferencing of its own). Default 1.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color\-fill
Disable color fill entirely, for a contour-only plot.
.TP
.B \-W\fP, \fB\-\-color\-control \fIspec\fP
Either \fIstyle\fP[\fB/\fP\fIpalette\fP[\fB/\fP\fIncolors\fP]] (e.g.
\fB1/2/11\fP: continuous style, palette 2, 11 colors), or the path to an
existing \fB.cpt\fP file to use as-is.
.TP
.B \-D\fP, \fB\-\-color\-flip
Reverse the color palette.
.TP
.B \-Y\fP, \fB\-\-no\-nice\-interval
Use a direct linear color stretch across the data range instead of a
rounded ("nice") interval.
.TP
.B \-\-stretch\-color
Histogram-equalize the color stretch (\fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 1 only).
.TP
.B \-Z\fP, \fB\-\-zbounds \fIzmin/zmax\fP
Override the grid's own detected z-range for every z-dependent
computation (color interval, contour interval, ...).
.TP
.B \-\-data\-scale \fIfactor\fP
Rescale grid values by \fIfactor\fP before colorizing/shading.
.TP
.B \-\-magnitude \fIval\fP, \fB\-\-azimuth \fIdeg\fP, \fB\-\-elevation \fIdeg\fP
Illumination/slope-shading parameters for \fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 2-5.
Defaults depend on the mode (see \fBmbm_grdplot\fP's \fB\-A\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-shade\-flip
Reverse the shading direction (negates the effective magnitude).
.TP
.B \-\-intensity\-file \fIgrid\fP
Intensity grid for \fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 3.
.TP
.B \-\-stretch\-shade
Histogram-equalize the intensity file first (\fB\-\-color\-mode\fP 3 only).
.TP
.B \-C\fP, \fB\-\-contour \fI[interval]\fP
Enable a \fBgrdcontour\fP overlay, at the given interval/spec/\fB.cpt\fP
path if supplied, otherwise at \fBmbm_grdplot\fP's own auto-computed
"reasonable" interval for the data range.
.TP
.B \-\-contour\-file \fIgrid\fP
Grid to contour, if different from \fB\-\-input\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-contour\-annotation \fIinterval\fP
Contour annotation interval (\fBmbm_grdplot\fP's \fB\-MCA\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-contour\-pen \fIpen\fP
Contour line pen (\fB\-MCW\fP). Default \fBc1p\fP (the regular, i.e.
non-annotated, contour pen at 1 point).
.TP
.B \-\-contour\-gap \fIspec\fP
Contour line gap spec (\fB\-MCG\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-contour\-cut \fIval\fP
Omit contour segments shorter than \fIval\fP (\fB\-MCQ\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-contour\-tick \fI[spacing]\fP
Add downhill-direction ticks to closed contours, optionally at the
given tick spacing (\fB\-MCT\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-coast
Enable a coastline overlay (\fBgmt coast\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-resolution \fI{f,h,i,l,c}\fP
Coastline database resolution: full, high, intermediate, low, crude.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-dry\-fill\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-wet\-fill\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-lake\-fill \fIcolor\fP
Fill colors for land, water, and lakes.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-river \fIcolor\fP
Draw rivers in the given color.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-boundary \fIspec\fP
Draw a national boundary; repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-pen \fIpen\fP
Pen for the coastline itself.
.TP
.B \-\-xy\-overlay \fIfile\fP[\fB:fill=\fP\fIfill\fP][\fB:symbol=\fP\fIsymbol\fP][\fB:pen=\fP\fIpen\fP]
Overlay an xy data file (\fBgmt plot\fP), with optional colon-separated
styling, e.g. \fBpoints.xy:fill=red:symbol=c0.1:pen=1p,blue\fP.
Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-text \fIlon/lat/size/angle/font/justify/text\fP
Place a text label (\fBgmt text\fP), e.g.
\fB\-122.2/36.6/12/0/1/LB/Monterey Bay\fP. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-nav\-file \fIdatalist\fP
MB-System swath datalist to plot navigation from, via MB-System's own
\fBgmt mbcontour\fP GMT supplement module.
.TP
.B \-\-nav\-format \fIfmt\fP
Datalist format code. Default: auto-detected via \fBmbformat\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-nav\-ticks \fIspec\fP
Tick/annotation spec, e.g. \fB0.25/1/4/0.15\fP, or \fBF\fP/\fBFP\fP to
annotate with the swath file name (perpendicular, for \fBFP\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-ping\-ticks \fItick/annot/len\fP
Ping-number annotation spec along the navigation track, e.g.
\fB50/100/0.1\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-nav\-pen \fIpen\fP
Pen for the navigation track line.
.TP
.B \-\-gmt\-default \fIparam/value\fP
Override a GMT default parameter for this plot (e.g.
\fBMAP_FRAME_TYPE/plain\fP); repeatable.

.SH EXAMPLES
Suppose one wants to generate a shaded-by-slope-magnitude topography
map with a swath navigation overlay, a distance scale bar, and a color
scale bar labeled in meters, rendered directly to a 300 dpi PNG:

.br
 mbpy_grdplot \-I topo.grd \-O topoplot \\
.br
     \-\-color\-mode 5 \-\-shade\-flip \-\-magnitude 1 \\
.br
     \-\-title "Survey Area" \-\-colorbar\-label "Topography (meters)" \\
.br
     \-\-length\-scale "fx10/2/32.70/5.0+lkm" \\
.br
     \-\-nav\-file datalist.mb\-1 \\
.br
     \-\-pagesize c \-\-dpi 300 \-\-format png \-\-execute \-V

This produces \fBtopoplot.sh\fP (the generated GMT modern-mode
shellscript), \fBtopoplot.cpt\fP (the color palette), and, because
\fB\-\-execute\fP was given, runs the script immediately to produce
\fBtopoplot.png\fP.

A plain color-fill map with a 100-meter contour overlay, written to a
script for later inspection/execution rather than run immediately:

.br
 mbpy_grdplot \-I topo.grd \-O topocont \\
.br
     \-\-color\-mode 1 \-\-contour 100 \-\-contour\-pen "0.5p,black" \\
.br
     \-\-title "Survey Area" \-\-colorbar\-label "Topography (meters)" \\
.br
     \-\-format pdf \-V

